[36m(TaskRunner pid=331456)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=331456)[0m We need to find the divisors of \(362880\) that are congruent to 1 modulo 10. These divisors must be co-prime to 10, meaning they cannot be divisible by 2 or 5. Therefore, we consider the part of the factorization excluding the primes 2 and 5, which gives us the number \(3^4 \times 7\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=331456)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=331456)[0m The number \(3^4 \times 7 = 81 \times 7 = 567\). The divisors of 567 are of the form \(3^a \times 7^b\) where \(0 \leq a \leq 4\) and \(0 \leq b \leq 1\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=331456)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=331456)[0m We check which of these divisors are congruent to 1 modulo 10:
