[36m(TaskRunner pid=331456)[0m We need the sum of the divisors of 9! that have units digit 1. These divisors must be congruent to 1 modulo 10. Such divisors must be coprime with 10, meaning they cannot have factors of 2 or 5. Therefore, we consider the divisors of \( 9! \) that are products of the factors 3, 7, and so on.
